                  "type": "intro",
                  "title": "Your RHIT Exam: 150 Questions Stand Between You and Your Credential",
                  "content": "The RHIT exam is the gateway to your career in Health Information Management. In 3.5 hours, you will face 150 multiple-choice questions -- but only 130 are scored. The other 20 are pretest items being evaluated for future exams, and you will never know which ones they are. That means you must treat EVERY question as if it counts. This lesson gives you the complete exam blueprint: how the test is structured, what each domain covers, how scoring works, and -- most importantly -- the test-taking strategies that separate those who pass from those who do not. The pass rate hovers around 70%, which means nearly 1 in 3 test-takers fail. You will not be one of them. Let's build your domination strategy.",
